WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.068
The takeaway: low rank and low precision are
complementary,

00:00:04.148 --> 00:00:06.739
and exploiting them together pays off.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:12.082
By sketching a matrix with a Gaussian projection
and quantizing the factors,

00:00:12.162 --> 00:00:17.566
LPLR compresses to one bit per coordinate while
preserving accuracy on images,

00:00:17.646 --> 00:00:21.503
embeddings, and LLM weights, with provable error bounds.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:25.580
And by avoiding costly SVD, it scales to largest matrices.
